# text = Miss Dombey , in her guileless innocent heart , regards me as her adopted brother ; but what would the guile and guilt of my heart be , if I pretended to believe that I had any right to approach her , familiarly , in that character -- if I pretended to forget that I am bound , in honour , not to do it Wal'r , my lad ain't there no other character as Oh would you have me die in her esteem -- in such esteem as hers -- and put a veil between myself and her angel's face for ever , by taking advantage of her being here for refuge , so trusting and so unprotected , to endeavour to exalt myself into her lover ?
